@startuml
title La Nonna - modelo de dominio y propiedad de datos
hide methods
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "Auth Service / auth_data" {
  class User {
    id: integer
    username: unique string
    password_hash: string
    password_salt: string
    role: user | admin
    full_name: string
  }
  class Session {
    id: integer
    user_id: integer
    token: unique string
    expires_at: datetime
  }
  User "1" -- "0..*" Session
}

package "Clients Service / clients_data" {
  class Client {
    id: integer
    user_id: integer
    username: string
    full_name: string
    email: unique string
    phone: string?
  }
}

package "Reservations Service / reservations_data" {
  class Reservation {
    id: integer
    user_id: integer?
    name: string
    email: string
    people: integer
    datetime: datetime
    status: string
  }
}

package "Inventory Service / inventory_data" {
  class Product {
    id: integer
    nombre: string
    descripcion: string
    precio: decimal
    categoria: string
    stock: integer
  }
  class StockReservation {
    reference: unique UUID
    items_json: JSON
    products_json: price/name snapshot
    status: reserved | released
  }
  class InventoryMovement {
    id: integer
    product_id: integer
    actor_user_id: integer
    quantity_delta: integer
    reason: string
  }
  Product "1" -- "0..*" InventoryMovement
  Product "1" -- "0..*" StockReservation : product IDs in snapshot
}

package "Orders Service / orders_data" {
  class Order {
    id: integer
    user_id: integer
    inventory_reference: unique UUID
    status: pending | confirmed | preparing | ready | completed | cancelled
    total: decimal
  }
  class OrderItem {
    id: integer
    product_id: integer
    product_name: string
    unit_price: decimal
    quantity: integer
  }
  Order "1" *-- "1..*" OrderItem
}

package "Payments Service / payments_data" {
  class Payment {
    id: integer
    order_id: integer
    user_id: integer
    amount: decimal
    status: pending | succeeded | failed | refunded
    provider: webpay-simulated
    provider_reference: unique string
    idempotency_key: unique string
  }
  class WebhookEvent {
    event_id: unique string
    payment_id: integer
    payload_hash: SHA-256
    status: pending | processed
  }
  Payment "1" -- "0..*" WebhookEvent
}

User ..> Client : user_id via registration contract
User ..> Order : user_id claim
User ..> Payment : user_id claim
User ..> Reservation : optional user_id claim
StockReservation ..> Order : inventory_reference
Order ..> Product : product_id + immutable snapshot
Payment ..> Order : HTTP contract; no cross-DB foreign key
Payment ..> OrderItem : amount validated via Orders API

note bottom
Cada servicio es dueño de su SQLite. Las relaciones entre paquetes
son referencias de identidad/contrato, no claves foráneas compartidas.
Orders solicita reserva/liberación idempotente a Inventory y guarda
su propio snapshot; fallos entre servicios se compensan, no son ACID global.
Webpay es un simulador ficticio: sin integración oficial ni cargos reales.
end note
@enduml
